WEBVTT

00:42.876 --> 00:46.004
"His drawings that show his emotions

00:46.087 --> 00:48.214
are just like doodles

00:48.298 --> 00:50.592
of a child trapped in his own world."

00:52.927 --> 00:55.263
My entire life was summed up

00:55.346 --> 00:56.973
into a sentence by someone else.

00:57.056 --> 00:58.683
It made me pity you.

01:00.727 --> 01:03.438
It seemed like
your life was so meaningless

01:04.689 --> 01:06.274
that you could abandon anything.

01:07.067 --> 01:10.361
What would be left of your life
if you lived like that?

01:11.196 --> 01:14.240
No one could have put it better than this.

01:14.324 --> 01:17.702
WITH UNG

01:19.287 --> 01:20.455
THE UNBEARABLE LIGHTNESS OF BEING

01:20.538 --> 01:23.750
I want to live a peaceful life
without doing anything.

01:25.877 --> 01:26.878
Ma'am.

01:26.961 --> 01:28.129
What's your rank?

01:28.213 --> 01:29.881
I'm 267th.

01:29.964 --> 01:31.466
The total number of students here…

01:31.549 --> 01:33.134
There are 267 students.

01:35.386 --> 01:37.180
Drawing is just going to be a hobby.

01:37.263 --> 01:38.681
You know my dream.

01:38.765 --> 01:42.519
It's to bask in the sun during the day
and to lie underneath a lamp at night.

01:42.602 --> 01:44.521
A stressful life is not for me.

01:47.565 --> 01:48.858
I can draw a new one.

01:48.942 --> 01:50.902
Do you have no ambitions?

01:51.986 --> 01:54.697
Give this chance to someone
who needs it more than I do.

01:55.615 --> 01:57.367
Your thoughts about your work,

01:57.450 --> 02:00.203
your life as an artist,

02:00.286 --> 02:01.871
or your future plans and goals.

02:04.207 --> 02:05.458
I don't have any.

02:06.709 --> 02:10.046
That was how I had lived all along.

02:12.549 --> 02:15.552
You're one lucky kid, aren't you?

02:15.635 --> 02:18.680
You have such successful parents.

02:18.763 --> 02:20.098
What do you want to be when you grow up?

02:20.181 --> 02:23.268
You can be anything you want
since money won't be an issue.

02:23.351 --> 02:25.270
Gosh, lucky you.

02:26.771 --> 02:28.940
That's it. Hold your spoon like this.

02:29.023 --> 02:32.068
Get a good spoonful of rice.

02:32.152 --> 02:35.113
All you have to do
is eat well and be healthy. Like this.

02:38.283 --> 02:39.367
- That's it.
- He's right.

02:39.450 --> 02:42.579
Don't you worry about a thing
and just do what you want in life.

02:42.662 --> 02:46.583
- That's all we want from you, okay?
- There you go.

02:47.500 --> 02:49.377
- Goodness.
- What a good boy.

02:49.460 --> 02:53.715
At times, nothing is the best you can do…

02:58.094 --> 03:01.639
when you're living a borrowed life.

03:04.267 --> 03:07.061
Ung, can you draw me?

03:07.145 --> 03:09.564
Ung, can you draw me first?

03:09.647 --> 03:13.151
- No. Ung, draw me--
- Ung, can you draw me first?

03:13.943 --> 03:16.738
- Ung, draw me first.
- No, draw me first.

03:16.821 --> 03:18.156
- So it's best…
- Come on.

03:18.239 --> 03:19.908
- …not to be greedy.
- Ung, draw me.

03:24.746 --> 03:28.124
Ung, when will you draw me?

03:28.833 --> 03:31.544
Ung, when will you draw me?

03:31.628 --> 03:33.630
Can you please draw me?

03:33.713 --> 03:34.881
I'll draw you.

03:34.964 --> 03:38.801
- But you can't draw.
- Who do you think he takes after?

03:38.885 --> 03:39.844
Me.

03:40.428 --> 03:43.306
That's good. You look beautiful.
Good. Stay still.

03:43.389 --> 03:46.476
Yes. You look great right now.

03:47.393 --> 03:52.774
I wanted to be a son
who was worthy of this perfect family…

03:52.857 --> 03:54.734
No, stop blinking.

03:59.989 --> 04:02.533
…and not a son
who was abandoned by their parents.

04:02.617 --> 04:06.204
It's so hectic around here
thanks to a group of customers.

04:06.871 --> 04:08.748
- Here.
- It's way too hectic.

04:09.332 --> 04:12.085
So if I didn't do anything,

04:12.168 --> 04:13.544
no one would know.

04:13.628 --> 04:15.255
A series of studies have claimed

04:15.338 --> 04:18.049
that one's genes have more effect

04:18.132 --> 04:23.429
on determining one's personality
than the environment.

04:23.513 --> 04:27.016
To support this theory,
gene-mapping researchers in the US

04:27.100 --> 04:31.104
are currently looking for the genes
that determine one's personality--

04:32.230 --> 04:34.023
- Honestly, I don't know either.
- Me too.

04:37.277 --> 04:41.197
Deep down, I was afraid
that I might be a worthless person.

04:43.116 --> 04:45.201
That's why
I pretended not to know anything

04:46.244 --> 04:48.413
and that I wasn't interested at all.

04:49.664 --> 04:50.832
But in the end,

04:51.874 --> 04:53.918
this is how things turned out.

04:56.421 --> 04:57.505
So now

04:58.631 --> 05:01.092
I've become a worthless person

05:02.010 --> 05:06.222
who's trapped in his own empty life.

05:06.306 --> 05:10.476
EPISODE 16
OUR BELOVED SUMMER

05:13.688 --> 05:17.817
ENROLLMENT GUIDE SCHOOL OF ARCHITECTURE
ENSA, PARIS

05:22.196 --> 05:24.532
I want to go with you.

05:35.001 --> 05:36.544
I'm not taking this lightly.

05:38.254 --> 05:40.089
I've thought this through for a while.

05:40.631 --> 05:44.093
I do understand
that this may seem sudden to you,

05:48.139 --> 05:50.099
but can you just trust me on this?

05:57.565 --> 06:01.694
So you were interested after all.

06:02.570 --> 06:05.281
I know my life has seemed pathetic.

06:07.075 --> 06:08.242
So…

06:09.702 --> 06:11.662
I'm going to start afresh.

06:14.165 --> 06:15.249
And…

06:16.334 --> 06:17.418
I need you by my side.

06:18.836 --> 06:21.130
I can't do this by myself.

06:24.258 --> 06:27.178
But to go this far away--

06:27.261 --> 06:28.763
I need you.

06:28.846 --> 06:29.972
You know that.

06:34.268 --> 06:37.313
Can you please come with me
and be with me?

06:43.152 --> 06:44.779
Because, you see,

06:45.696 --> 06:47.198
I'm a bit of a mess right now.

06:58.251 --> 06:59.627
I'll think about it.

07:00.711 --> 07:01.796
Give me some time.

07:05.883 --> 07:07.677
I'll give it some thought.

07:08.803 --> 07:09.929
Really?

07:11.430 --> 07:12.390
Yes.

07:13.391 --> 07:16.894
After all, this is the first time
you found something you wanted to do.

07:21.399 --> 07:23.025
Did I seem too weak?

07:23.985 --> 07:25.069
No.

07:25.736 --> 07:28.239
And I never thought you were pathetic.

07:28.739 --> 07:31.242
You've achieved more than I have.

07:47.300 --> 07:50.094
Sorry? What did you just say?

07:52.597 --> 07:55.391
I'd like you to work
at our headquarters in Paris.

07:56.350 --> 07:59.770
I've been assigned there recently
and need to build a new team.

07:59.854 --> 08:02.064
And you were the first one I thought of.

08:02.607 --> 08:05.943
I looked through all your past projects,
and they were quite fascinating.

08:07.195 --> 08:08.446
But why me?

08:08.529 --> 08:10.907
You're someone I need, Ms. Kook.

08:13.075 --> 08:15.411
So I'd like you to come with me.

08:22.084 --> 08:25.588
The terms are quite favorable.
I'm actively trying to recruit you

08:25.671 --> 08:28.591
because I know how competent you are.

08:30.843 --> 08:32.094
Thank you.

08:32.678 --> 08:35.264
I didn't expect you
of all people to make such an offer.

08:35.348 --> 08:37.934
I don't know what to think.

08:38.518 --> 08:40.019
Do I still seem like a sociopath?

08:42.063 --> 08:43.356
I should get going.

08:44.357 --> 08:46.275
I need to walk my dog.

08:46.359 --> 08:48.152
Think about it and call me.

09:05.211 --> 09:06.504
It's a good opportunity.

09:06.587 --> 09:09.882
Mr. Jang came to me first
and told me about it.

09:10.508 --> 09:13.177
He sure has a keen eye for talent.

09:13.844 --> 09:17.390
Anyway, don't think about it too much
and just do it, okay?

09:17.473 --> 09:19.892
- No. I--
- Yeon-su.

09:20.685 --> 09:24.230
I'm saying this
as a colleague who truly cares about you.

09:24.313 --> 09:26.524
I truly want you
to seize this opportunity.

09:27.233 --> 09:30.695
I saw how hard you worked to get this far.

09:30.778 --> 09:34.865
So this time around,
put yourself first before anyone else.

09:34.949 --> 09:38.911
You should also live the life
you want, right?

09:57.763 --> 09:59.557
How could he fire me like this?

10:00.308 --> 10:02.685
I'm going to report him
to the Ministry of Employment and Labor.

10:03.394 --> 10:08.190
I'm going to expose everything
he's done and sue him.

10:08.274 --> 10:09.984
I know you won't do that.

10:10.568 --> 10:12.028
Choi Ung, you scumbag.

10:12.862 --> 10:14.614
He can't do anything without me.

10:14.697 --> 10:16.157
Let's see how well he does.

10:16.240 --> 10:18.826
What can you do? He wants to go.

10:19.744 --> 10:22.246
Tag along with him
if you're that sad to say goodbye.

10:22.330 --> 10:24.790
He didn't even bother to invite me.

10:25.583 --> 10:27.001
Had he asked,

10:27.084 --> 10:29.545
I would have pretended
it was a dilemma then gave in.

10:30.212 --> 10:31.922
I can't believe him.

10:33.633 --> 10:35.384
But what can you do in France?

10:35.468 --> 10:37.178
Isn't he going there to study?

10:37.261 --> 10:39.889
Then he must've made
that decision for your sake.

10:39.972 --> 10:42.350
Look. He told me to live my life.

10:42.433 --> 10:46.354
So is he saying I haven't been living
my life this whole time?

10:46.437 --> 10:49.148
And does he think
I can't do anything without him?

10:50.650 --> 10:52.151
What will you do without him?

10:53.235 --> 10:54.278
Without him, I'll…

10:56.155 --> 10:57.156
I'll…

10:58.783 --> 11:01.911
I can't do anything without him…

11:07.833 --> 11:08.834
DAEHAN BANK

11:09.418 --> 11:11.253
What is this?

11:16.258 --> 11:17.426
What's wrong?

11:17.927 --> 11:19.637
What is it?

11:19.720 --> 11:20.596
Come on.

11:23.015 --> 11:26.060
- Are these tears or snot?
- My severance pay…

11:26.644 --> 11:27.853
Your nose is running.

11:27.937 --> 11:29.688
- My severance pay…
- What?

11:29.772 --> 11:31.649
- My severance pay…
- What about it?

11:31.732 --> 11:33.234
Is he not giving you any?

11:33.317 --> 11:35.236
He gave me too much…

11:46.705 --> 11:47.706
No way!

11:56.298 --> 11:57.466
Eun-ho.

11:58.008 --> 11:59.885
If you don't have any future plans,

12:00.386 --> 12:03.931
how about we start a business together?

12:05.057 --> 12:06.016
Don't be absurd.

12:06.892 --> 12:08.394
I don't do business with others.

12:12.481 --> 12:14.525
I already got a friend discount.

12:15.734 --> 12:17.278
So how about a celebrity discount?

12:18.279 --> 12:20.948
- I can give you a bigger discount.
- That's not right.

12:21.490 --> 12:24.410
You should stop saying things
that lower the value of your work.

12:24.493 --> 12:26.996
They're not that great to begin with.

12:29.748 --> 12:34.378
What? Are you saying
that I have terrible taste in art?

12:35.045 --> 12:36.630
No, that's not what I meant.

12:36.714 --> 12:39.049
Do you know why I like your drawings?

12:40.301 --> 12:42.428
The more I looked at them,
the more I realized

12:43.053 --> 12:45.848
why your drawings comforted me.

12:46.432 --> 12:48.517
The winding lines made me wonder

12:50.060 --> 12:54.106
if you were just as anxious as I was.

12:55.107 --> 12:57.776
Your stubbornness
to only draw things that didn't change

12:58.611 --> 13:02.198
made me wonder
if you were just as lonely as I was.

13:04.533 --> 13:07.244
But whenever I look at your finished work,

13:08.829 --> 13:10.372
it warms my heart.

13:11.415 --> 13:12.666
It puts me at ease.

13:14.126 --> 13:16.587
You seem like someone

13:18.088 --> 13:19.840
who's strong inside.

13:24.011 --> 13:26.180
And, surprisingly,
they end up comforting me.

13:27.723 --> 13:30.309
It's as if you're saying
that I can become like you.

13:34.897 --> 13:38.734
This is my criticism of your work.

13:39.818 --> 13:42.196
So don't mind the others
and just listen to me.

13:42.279 --> 13:44.240
After all, I'm your biggest buyer.

13:45.449 --> 13:46.617
Thank you.

13:47.243 --> 13:49.745
Your words are surprisingly comforting.

13:51.747 --> 13:55.584
We must've become really close,
seeing how we're comforting each other.

14:00.464 --> 14:03.759
Anyway, I'm sad to hear you'll be leaving.

14:04.760 --> 14:06.929
Studying abroad can be very lonely.

14:07.429 --> 14:09.723
Yeon-su will be coming with me.

14:12.560 --> 14:13.769
Really?

14:14.270 --> 14:15.771
I can't live without her.

14:16.355 --> 14:17.231
I see.

14:18.816 --> 14:20.401
She must…

14:22.194 --> 14:24.029
really love you

14:25.906 --> 14:30.202
to choose your life over hers.

14:31.328 --> 14:33.289
That's not easy to do.

14:44.383 --> 14:45.467
Grandma.

14:46.510 --> 14:47.678
Yes?

14:48.679 --> 14:51.015
Will you really be okay without me?

14:51.098 --> 14:53.475
Of course. I'll be just fine.

14:54.602 --> 14:56.645
That was quick.

14:57.146 --> 14:58.522
That hurt.

14:59.940 --> 15:04.486
I can keep myself busy
by spending time with the old ladies.

15:04.570 --> 15:08.240
But what if you collapse again?

15:08.324 --> 15:12.912
They said I'd be fine as long as I take
my blood pressure medication regularly.

15:12.995 --> 15:14.163
Goodness.

15:16.081 --> 15:18.083
So stop worrying about me

15:18.667 --> 15:22.296
and follow your heart.

15:26.675 --> 15:29.053
That's a favor I'm asking of you. Got it?

15:33.057 --> 15:34.058
Let's go.

15:34.141 --> 15:35.851
Goodness. Let's go.

15:36.894 --> 15:37.770
Let's go.

15:43.192 --> 15:47.363
…To choose your life over hers.

15:48.030 --> 15:51.408
After all, this is the first time
you found something you wanted to do.

16:28.487 --> 16:32.074
You should also live the life
you want, right?

16:33.534 --> 16:36.870
So stop worrying about me

16:36.954 --> 16:38.580
and follow your heart.

16:40.666 --> 16:42.543
Follow my heart?

16:57.725 --> 17:04.440
DAILYBEER

17:12.531 --> 17:14.616
Thank you. Enjoy.

17:21.915 --> 17:23.208
Do it.

17:23.876 --> 17:25.711
Why should I?

17:26.295 --> 17:27.546
That's what we do.

17:28.380 --> 17:30.507
Recording the moments of people's lives.

17:31.341 --> 17:35.054
We explain how priceless
that is time after time to those we film,

17:35.137 --> 17:37.890
so why won't you do it?

17:37.973 --> 17:39.975
There isn't anything worth recording.

17:45.898 --> 17:46.940
You know what?

17:48.400 --> 17:49.526
I just don't get it.

17:51.028 --> 17:54.281
She came back because she's dying
when she's ignored me all my life.

17:54.865 --> 17:56.283
This is just absurd.

17:57.117 --> 18:00.037
What should I do?

18:01.455 --> 18:03.290
Why should I…

18:05.167 --> 18:07.169
do this for her?

18:09.671 --> 18:11.548
I just don't get it.

18:12.549 --> 18:14.134
Do it for yourself.

18:16.762 --> 18:18.972
You're the one
who'll have to live with it.

18:19.056 --> 18:22.851
The one who'll have
to live with those memories.

18:24.144 --> 18:25.479
is you.

18:33.153 --> 18:34.238
Hey.

18:34.947 --> 18:37.783
Do you even have a portrait
you can use for her funeral?

18:41.328 --> 18:42.412
Funny, right?

18:43.288 --> 18:47.126
You run around with a camera all the time
yet you don't have one photo of your mom.

18:48.836 --> 18:52.047
I only have one photo of my mom.

18:52.131 --> 18:54.675
But it's a group photo.

18:56.260 --> 18:59.930
She's surrounded by others
and smiling from ear to ear.

19:02.432 --> 19:04.601
I'm grateful to have even that.

19:05.978 --> 19:08.647
I look at it at times when I think of her.

19:16.071 --> 19:19.158
I don't know your story.

19:19.658 --> 19:23.787
Whether you decide to resent her
or forgive her, save that for later.

19:23.871 --> 19:29.626
I just hope you won't
waste this moment by not doing anything.

19:32.296 --> 19:33.297
That's all.

20:26.475 --> 20:28.185
- Ung.
- Yes?

20:29.228 --> 20:30.938
Do you want to…

20:32.564 --> 20:34.483
meet up at Sol-i's later this evening?

20:36.902 --> 20:37.986
Sure.

20:59.591 --> 21:01.385
Okay. I understand.

21:01.885 --> 21:03.845
I respect your decision.

21:18.318 --> 21:19.319
Come on.

21:19.403 --> 21:22.614
The owner here
sure makes her customers uncomfortable.

21:22.698 --> 21:25.617
She needs to take
a close look at this one customer

21:25.701 --> 21:27.995
since he rarely visits.

21:29.913 --> 21:33.083
You must be busy dating,
so what brings you all the way here?

21:34.334 --> 21:36.545
No particular reason.
I just missed your food.

21:42.926 --> 21:44.761
Gosh. I'm not a kid anymore.

21:51.977 --> 21:55.105
When you're going through a lot,
you should eat well.

21:55.188 --> 21:57.107
I never said I was.

21:57.190 --> 21:59.276
But as your mom, I can tell.

22:08.076 --> 22:09.036
My son.

22:10.662 --> 22:12.331
I can't believe you're all grown up.

22:34.644 --> 22:36.188
You knew…

22:37.314 --> 22:38.356
Yes.

22:39.024 --> 22:40.692
I did.

22:43.070 --> 22:44.613
…that I knew

22:53.080 --> 22:56.333
Did anything change because of that?

22:57.584 --> 22:58.960
Why would it?

22:59.669 --> 23:02.714
You're my son no matter what.

23:06.510 --> 23:11.681
You were always my son, Ung.

23:17.270 --> 23:19.022
Thank you for being my son.

23:19.898 --> 23:23.985
I'm truly grateful
that you grew up into a wonderful man.

23:33.578 --> 23:34.663
I…

23:40.836 --> 23:42.546
I was afraid…

23:45.006 --> 23:47.259
that I wouldn't take after you and Dad.

23:56.601 --> 23:59.980
I was afraid I wouldn't turn out
to be a good person like you.

24:05.318 --> 24:07.320
That I might end up being a bad apple…

24:10.073 --> 24:11.825
and fail to live up to your expectations.

24:13.451 --> 24:15.203
I was afraid

24:16.079 --> 24:17.789
that you might be disappointed in me.

24:19.374 --> 24:21.042
That was my biggest fear.

24:24.004 --> 24:25.755
What should I say?

24:27.257 --> 24:30.677
Your dad and I
were never disappointed in you.

24:34.848 --> 24:38.560
Since the moment we held you in our arms,

24:40.270 --> 24:42.480
we've loved every part of you.

25:05.670 --> 25:06.755
Mom.

25:06.838 --> 25:08.006
Yes?

25:08.089 --> 25:09.216
I want

25:09.925 --> 25:12.344
to become a better version of myself.

25:13.136 --> 25:14.930
I wish that you could…

25:16.932 --> 25:19.726
sleep in peace now.

25:27.609 --> 25:30.862
Eat up. You should have this
while it's still hot.

25:36.493 --> 25:39.037
NJ, this is your last interview.

25:40.038 --> 25:42.999
We've prepared the questions beforehand.

25:43.083 --> 25:45.377
You can answer them comfortably.

25:45.460 --> 25:49.005
First, we'd like you to explain

25:49.089 --> 25:52.217
why you wanted to shoot here
for your last interview.

25:52.300 --> 25:55.720
Sir, I have a favor to ask.

25:55.804 --> 25:56.763
Sure.

25:57.514 --> 25:58.515
What is it?

26:12.279 --> 26:14.739
- Did you wait long?
- No, not really.

26:16.449 --> 26:17.742
Isn't it really cold out?

26:17.826 --> 26:19.494
Yes, it's freezing.

26:21.413 --> 26:23.581
I told you to wear thicker clothes.

26:24.082 --> 26:25.959
I warmed up my hands for you.

26:26.668 --> 26:27.919
- Are they warm?
- Yes.

26:28.545 --> 26:31.339
But I'm really fine.
Your hands will become cold again.

26:31.923 --> 26:32.924
That's okay.

26:40.181 --> 26:41.641
I guess you've made up

26:42.767 --> 26:43.643
your mind.

26:45.520 --> 26:46.521
Yes.

27:12.297 --> 27:15.675
I knew it. She's always waiting for me.

27:43.787 --> 27:44.954
Grandma.

27:49.250 --> 27:51.294
Remember what you told me?

27:54.005 --> 27:56.800
You told me
to stop enduring everything on my own.

27:58.635 --> 28:00.720
And to make friends,

28:02.263 --> 28:04.057
follow my heart,

28:05.016 --> 28:06.476
and enjoy life.

28:09.437 --> 28:11.272
So this time around,

28:12.816 --> 28:14.692
I'm going to be bold

28:16.361 --> 28:18.696
and follow my heart.

28:22.075 --> 28:24.327
But you know what?

28:25.745 --> 28:28.456
I realized I had been living
like that all along.

28:31.835 --> 28:35.046
I always thought I was alone.

28:38.007 --> 28:39.217
But…

28:42.011 --> 28:44.389
there was never a time when I was alone.

29:06.494 --> 29:07.412
Hey.

29:08.913 --> 29:10.290
- Welcome…
- Hey.

29:13.376 --> 29:16.004
Hey, I came up with a scenario.

29:16.087 --> 29:17.756
Give me an objective review.

29:17.839 --> 29:19.466
He asked for my number in public.

29:19.549 --> 29:23.553
It's called Omniscient Psychopath's View…
…And he looked pretty sincere.

29:24.804 --> 29:27.390
I have an offer to make.

29:27.474 --> 29:30.226
Yi-hoon, I'm too busy to make time--

29:30.310 --> 29:31.978
Would you like to work with me?

29:33.646 --> 29:35.523
I'm sorry, but I'm too busy.

29:35.607 --> 29:37.400
I'm not just asking for your help.

29:37.484 --> 29:39.527
I'm recruiting you.

29:41.029 --> 29:43.865
I started a company,
and the terms are not bad at all.

29:45.325 --> 29:48.203
Right. There's also an advance payment.

29:51.748 --> 29:55.084
I never asked for your help.

29:55.835 --> 29:59.964
I know you'll land a job
at a big corporate company

30:00.048 --> 30:01.925
if you take your time and prepare for it.

30:02.008 --> 30:03.718
My company is small, I know.

30:03.802 --> 30:08.181
But I'm going to give you a lot of work
and get my money's worth.

30:08.264 --> 30:09.599
What I'm saying is

30:10.183 --> 30:14.395
that I'm trying to make
the biggest investment of my life on you.

30:15.647 --> 30:17.440
Read this through.

30:18.024 --> 30:20.735
Call me if you change your mind.
Goodbye, then.

30:21.319 --> 30:23.446
Right. Thanks for the coffee.

30:36.042 --> 30:38.253
CONTRACT
RUN AND GOOK YEON-SU'S AGREEMENT

30:40.630 --> 30:41.673
ON AND OFFLINE PR PLANS

30:50.390 --> 30:51.432
- Yeon-su.
- Yes?

30:51.516 --> 30:54.769
Can you include this part? It's important.

30:54.853 --> 30:56.521
Got it? Okay?

30:56.604 --> 30:59.148
We need to collaborate.

31:00.608 --> 31:02.068
Ms. Kook!

31:02.151 --> 31:04.195
- Ms. Kook!
- Ma'am, your presentation was awesome.

31:04.279 --> 31:06.281
It was such a clean-cut presentation.

31:06.364 --> 31:07.407
I think we'll succeed again.

31:07.490 --> 31:08.867
You're the best!

31:08.950 --> 31:10.910
Being surprised by you is getting old.

31:10.994 --> 31:13.788
How do you keep getting better?

31:15.999 --> 31:18.918
I'm right, aren't I?

31:19.419 --> 31:21.504
- Get-together tonight?
- Sure thing!

31:22.714 --> 31:25.258
I thought my life was pretty dull.

31:31.973 --> 31:34.017
But, actually,

31:35.602 --> 31:37.437
I've always had pretty good moments.

31:38.855 --> 31:41.274
The only person
who made my life seem pathetic…

31:44.402 --> 31:45.945
was just me.

31:47.989 --> 31:49.157
Grandma.

32:10.929 --> 32:12.096
I'm not going,

32:13.306 --> 32:14.223
Ung.

32:19.771 --> 32:21.439
For the first time,

32:22.440 --> 32:24.943
I'm beginning to enjoy my life.

32:25.944 --> 32:27.320
For the first time in my life,

32:28.029 --> 32:30.406
I can clearly see the path I took.

32:31.991 --> 32:35.286
So I want to live this life a bit longer.

32:38.498 --> 32:40.124
I had always believed

32:41.584 --> 32:45.588
that I had no choice
but to live this life.

32:48.007 --> 32:49.342
But now…

32:50.969 --> 32:53.638
I think this was the life
I had always wanted.

32:55.598 --> 32:56.683
So…

32:58.226 --> 33:01.521
I want to keep exploring
the life I have now and keep going.

33:10.279 --> 33:11.948
Why aren't you saying anything?

33:14.951 --> 33:17.036
I was thinking about how long it'd take.

33:19.372 --> 33:20.665
What do you mean?

33:22.125 --> 33:24.752
How long it'd take for me

33:26.254 --> 33:28.047
to deserve you.

33:30.550 --> 33:31.801
What do you mean?

33:33.803 --> 33:36.931
You're an exceptional person
who exceeds my expectations.

33:38.725 --> 33:39.976
But, on the other hand,

33:41.853 --> 33:43.938
I've wasted too much time.

33:46.190 --> 33:47.400
Yeon-su.

33:49.610 --> 33:52.113
I've finally realized what I need to do.

33:53.322 --> 33:55.283
What I wanted to do,

33:56.034 --> 33:57.702
what I desire,

34:00.830 --> 34:02.665
and what kind of a person I am.

34:09.297 --> 34:10.590
So…

34:11.883 --> 34:13.051
I think I will…

34:15.386 --> 34:17.180
It's okay, Ung.

34:30.568 --> 34:31.736
You can go.

34:32.945 --> 34:34.489
We'll be fine.

34:43.539 --> 34:45.333
It won't take too long.

34:47.126 --> 34:48.127
I know.

34:49.128 --> 34:50.797
And I won't change either.

34:53.633 --> 34:54.842
I know.

34:56.928 --> 34:58.721
I will come back.

35:02.058 --> 35:03.142
I know.

35:05.603 --> 35:06.729
So…

35:10.191 --> 35:11.859
please wait for me.

35:55.194 --> 35:56.737
Come in.

35:56.821 --> 35:58.656
Why are you just standing there?

36:00.491 --> 36:03.119
This was always the distance between us.

36:04.203 --> 36:07.039
So why are you doing this now?

36:09.917 --> 36:11.169
It's unfair for me…

36:14.005 --> 36:15.882
to just die like this.

36:17.091 --> 36:19.635
If I died like this…

36:21.345 --> 36:23.139
without a trace,

36:23.931 --> 36:25.016
that'd be too unfair.

36:28.102 --> 36:29.312
You're selfish

36:30.605 --> 36:32.273
as always.

36:34.400 --> 36:35.651
Let me be…

36:40.281 --> 36:42.074
a terrible mom until the day I die.

36:42.742 --> 36:45.328
So don't mind me.

36:46.245 --> 36:49.957
You can feel a bit sorry for me

36:50.833 --> 36:51.751
and…

36:54.295 --> 36:55.796
visit me from time to time.

36:56.923 --> 36:58.132
Let's do that.

37:18.903 --> 37:20.613
That doesn't make any sense.

37:21.530 --> 37:24.033
Why would you come back
if that's what you wanted?

37:25.159 --> 37:27.203
If you wanted things to remain the same,

37:27.286 --> 37:29.538
you shouldn't have come back.

37:37.213 --> 37:38.714
Say something…

37:41.759 --> 37:42.927
will you?

37:45.221 --> 37:46.472
Please.

37:54.772 --> 37:56.023
Back then…

37:58.651 --> 38:02.154
the sickness I had in my heart
was too much to handle.

38:02.238 --> 38:03.864
I had no other choice.

38:06.284 --> 38:07.785
I was afraid

38:08.661 --> 38:13.374
you'd become as miserable as me
if you had stayed with me.

38:15.876 --> 38:17.128
At times…

38:20.089 --> 38:22.133
I'd see you outside…

38:23.843 --> 38:25.594
and you'd look so bright.

38:28.806 --> 38:30.683
I was afraid…

38:32.810 --> 38:34.895
I'd drag you down with me.

38:36.897 --> 38:38.774
I was so scared. That's why…

38:40.651 --> 38:43.946
That's why I couldn't embrace you.

38:51.662 --> 38:53.414
I won't forgive you.

38:54.915 --> 38:56.125
No.

38:58.377 --> 38:59.545
I can't.

39:02.089 --> 39:03.174
I understand.

39:04.508 --> 39:06.344
Your suffering…

39:10.014 --> 39:12.266
can't justify what you did to me.

39:14.935 --> 39:15.936
I know.

39:17.313 --> 39:18.314
Still…

39:20.483 --> 39:21.942
you were the mother.

39:26.697 --> 39:28.157
And…

39:30.159 --> 39:31.744
I was just a little kid.

39:33.496 --> 39:35.998
How could a mother do such a thing?

39:38.626 --> 39:39.835
You're right.

39:39.919 --> 39:43.756
How could you come back
and tell me that you're dying?

39:48.969 --> 39:52.264
I won't forgive you.

39:54.600 --> 39:55.434
Never.

39:57.561 --> 39:58.813
Okay.

40:01.273 --> 40:02.483
But…

40:04.693 --> 40:06.153
maybe one day…

40:08.989 --> 40:10.950
I might change my mind.

40:12.910 --> 40:14.036
So…

40:17.748 --> 40:19.333
fight to live.

40:21.752 --> 40:25.214
Both you and I can start anew.

40:26.424 --> 40:28.968
Let's not rely on others.

40:31.971 --> 40:34.098
Let's live an ordinary life…

40:36.350 --> 40:37.852
like everyone else does.

40:54.410 --> 40:57.204
We were 29 years old.

40:57.997 --> 41:00.166
That's when it all happened.

41:03.252 --> 41:06.839
And I was preparing to leave soon.

41:10.384 --> 41:11.844
I told my parents right away too.

41:11.927 --> 41:13.929
I'm leaving at the end of the month.

41:14.889 --> 41:15.806
Wait.

41:16.682 --> 41:17.892
Honey.

41:18.559 --> 41:23.272
Surprisingly, my dad got mad
and refused to see me for a while.

41:23.355 --> 41:26.150
Even though he did nothing
but nag me all this time.

41:34.658 --> 41:36.285
YOU'VE LEFT ME,
BUT I'M SENDING THIS FOR YOU

41:36.368 --> 41:38.329
Gu Eun-ho, who was also mad at me,

41:38.412 --> 41:41.540
sent me a 60-page document.

41:42.041 --> 41:44.919
Right. Ji-ung was busy.

41:45.669 --> 41:47.588
He said he was being filmed.

41:47.671 --> 41:49.173
I'm…

41:50.174 --> 41:51.133
So…

41:53.135 --> 41:54.637
What was the question again?

41:54.720 --> 41:59.642
What was the most memorable thing
you did with your mom, Mr. Kim?

42:00.726 --> 42:01.810
All right.

42:03.771 --> 42:04.813
Most memorable?

42:05.397 --> 42:08.734
I know.
I think every last Saturday of the month…

42:10.402 --> 42:13.572
we would go to the marketplace
and have tteokbokki together.

42:13.656 --> 42:17.952
I think that was the only day she had off.

42:20.412 --> 42:22.873
We'd hold hands and walk around.

42:23.958 --> 42:25.501
It made me happy.

42:26.001 --> 42:29.588
He always talked about being an observer.

42:29.672 --> 42:32.299
But he's finally been put in our shoes.

42:35.094 --> 42:37.805
I hope you won't forget

42:37.888 --> 42:40.933
- that living a normal life…
- NJ caused her agency another headache.

42:41.016 --> 42:44.019
I always wanted
to show you my cheerful side.

42:44.103 --> 42:46.522
But that had been eating me up inside.

42:46.605 --> 42:49.108
A 30-minute unedited video

42:49.191 --> 42:52.319
- was broadcast out of the blue.
- Let's be friends like that.

42:54.113 --> 42:56.657
The public seemed to be
outraged at her again,

42:56.740 --> 42:58.659
but she received a lot of support too.

43:00.244 --> 43:01.912
As for Yeon-su and I…

43:01.996 --> 43:03.080
Ung.

43:10.713 --> 43:12.089
- Weren't you cold?
- I'm fine.

43:12.172 --> 43:14.216
- Did I keep you waiting?
- Not at all.

43:14.300 --> 43:15.634
Let's go.

43:15.718 --> 43:17.595
We made the best of our time.

43:32.776 --> 43:35.112
We lived like that every day.

43:35.195 --> 43:38.449
By the way, did you really rehearse
spraying me with water?

43:38.532 --> 43:41.910
I was originally going to pour a bucket,
but I held myself back.

43:41.994 --> 43:43.245
Don't you dare do that again.

43:44.038 --> 43:46.290
You're making me curious.

43:46.874 --> 43:49.793
I take that back.
Don't do that again. Ever.

43:49.877 --> 43:51.086
No more what-ifs.

43:52.212 --> 43:54.798
Can I ask you one last what-if question?

43:54.882 --> 43:57.509
- There you go again.
- What if I…

43:58.385 --> 44:00.137
- Every single day.
- What if…

44:00.220 --> 44:01.263
- Hey.
- …you go abroad…

44:21.742 --> 44:22.993
It was perfect.

44:24.578 --> 44:27.998
- And I had to leave soon after.
- Ung.

44:28.082 --> 44:29.541
We're in huge trouble!

44:29.625 --> 44:32.628
- What is it?
- Hey, this is bad. It's terrible!

44:32.711 --> 44:33.629
What is it?

44:34.546 --> 44:36.590
- What's wrong?
- We've run out of gas.

44:37.257 --> 44:38.801
We'll be late if we stop for gas.

44:38.884 --> 44:42.054
You can't be late for your flight,
so how about you just don't go?

44:42.721 --> 44:45.474
Dad, I can see that the tank is full.

44:45.557 --> 44:47.309
And we still have a lot of time.

44:50.062 --> 44:53.148
Right. I have to stop by somewhere.

44:53.232 --> 44:54.191
Wait for me outside.

44:55.067 --> 44:58.070
Hey, Son. Then go wherever
you need to go and don't come back.

44:58.153 --> 45:01.907
Don't come back
so you can miss the flight, okay?

45:02.699 --> 45:03.742
I won't be long.

45:06.995 --> 45:11.208
There was one last thing I had to do
before starting my new journey.

45:16.004 --> 45:18.173
Confronting my past…

45:19.716 --> 45:21.218
that had been haunting me.

45:32.229 --> 45:34.523
I wanted to tell him once and for all…

45:35.899 --> 45:38.235
that there was no need for him
to keep hurting because of me,

45:38.318 --> 45:39.945
and that he didn't need to

45:40.654 --> 45:42.239
avoid me or feel sorry for me.

45:48.620 --> 45:50.247
That he had done enough,

45:51.957 --> 45:54.209
and that we should let go of each other.

46:03.927 --> 46:07.764
Like that, Ung left
around the end of winter.

46:12.978 --> 46:14.855
I was okay.

46:15.439 --> 46:18.150
You see, I like to be
in a mature relationship.

46:19.318 --> 46:22.779
I miss Ung. My dear Ung.

46:22.863 --> 46:25.199
Ung…

46:25.282 --> 46:27.201
- No…
- Can you call the police?

46:28.118 --> 46:30.996
I'm going to put her behind bars tonight.

46:31.079 --> 46:34.541
Ung! My dear Ung!

46:34.625 --> 46:37.085
- Of course, there were a few days…
- Find my dear Ung.

46:37.169 --> 46:40.547
- …when I missed him a bit too much.
- What are we to do with her?

46:43.342 --> 46:46.595
What if a foreign female student
who lives next door

46:46.678 --> 46:50.516
knocks on your door
and asks for some butter?

46:51.391 --> 46:53.519
I'm going to lock the door
and call the police.

46:53.602 --> 46:54.728
That's it.

46:56.021 --> 46:57.564
Then what if

46:57.648 --> 47:00.067
a fellow female student

47:00.150 --> 47:02.778
offers to teach you French?

47:02.861 --> 47:04.029
What will you do?

47:04.112 --> 47:05.864
I will show her my translating device.

47:05.948 --> 47:08.450
Good. You're doing well, Ung.

47:09.034 --> 47:11.245
Then what if you went to a coffee shop…

47:11.328 --> 47:13.914
Things are going fairly smoothly.

47:15.874 --> 47:19.253
Ms. Ji, can you share
the presentation materials with the team?

47:19.336 --> 47:20.546
Yes, ma'am.

47:20.629 --> 47:23.048
What's going on, you guys?

47:23.131 --> 47:27.010
How are you all so great at your jobs?

47:28.220 --> 47:30.556
I'm so happy.
I can't hold myself back anymore.

47:30.639 --> 47:32.266
- Let's--
- No get-togethers.

47:33.267 --> 47:34.726
I didn't say anything.

47:34.810 --> 47:36.395
We had one yesterday.

47:36.478 --> 47:38.730
Keep this up,
and I'll ban get-togethers again.

47:38.814 --> 47:40.774
"I'll ban get-togethers again." Geez.

47:41.275 --> 47:43.360
Then how about tomorrow evening?

47:43.443 --> 47:44.611
Tomorrow is Saturday.

47:44.695 --> 47:46.655
Then the coming Monday sounds good, right?

47:46.738 --> 47:49.408
We have a meeting. Not you, though.

47:49.491 --> 47:50.576
I see.

47:51.577 --> 47:52.452
Without me?

47:53.412 --> 47:54.705
You've planned a meeting.

47:54.788 --> 47:57.165
Did you all know
that I wouldn't be attending it?

47:57.249 --> 48:03.380
We focused on our lives and did our best
and time flew by.

48:04.339 --> 48:08.969
So why did you have
to drink so much in a foreign country?

48:09.052 --> 48:11.221
Do you know
how dangerous it could have been?

48:11.305 --> 48:12.681
- Of course…
- What then?

48:12.764 --> 48:14.933
…there were times when we bickered.

48:16.435 --> 48:19.104
So he's decided not to call me all day.

48:20.480 --> 48:23.108
I won't pick up even if you call.

48:29.448 --> 48:31.491
Hello? Ung?

48:31.575 --> 48:33.702
Hey. Have you been waiting for me?

48:34.453 --> 48:36.121
No, I wasn't waiting.

48:36.204 --> 48:38.498
Me? For your call? No. Not at all.

48:39.416 --> 48:41.627
Sorry. I was quite busy.

48:42.294 --> 48:46.590
Hey, I told you communication was the core
of a long-distance relationship.

48:46.673 --> 48:50.719
If this continues, I'll be really hurt
and it could cause a misunderstanding.

48:50.802 --> 48:53.055
I understand. Are you going home?

48:53.138 --> 48:56.016
Yes. What about you? Are you home?

48:56.099 --> 48:59.978
What about sleep? Did you sleep yet?
Did you eat? Did you eat on time?

49:00.062 --> 49:02.648
Aren't you tired of asking
the same thing every day?

49:02.731 --> 49:05.692
Tired? Are you tired of me?

49:05.776 --> 49:07.944
That's not what I meant.

49:08.028 --> 49:12.324
Geez, Yeon-su.
You seem to get annoyed so often.

49:12.407 --> 49:14.993
You're right. I've become petty.

49:16.703 --> 49:18.080
Had I known I'd be like this,

49:18.163 --> 49:20.999
I would've hidden
your passport when you flew in last time.

49:23.168 --> 49:24.670
You've become cuter too.

49:26.755 --> 49:28.799
I miss you, Ung.

49:31.593 --> 49:34.721
What? Why aren't you saying anything?

49:34.805 --> 49:35.972
Yeon-su.

49:36.640 --> 49:40.018
Now that I think about it,
there was something I forgot to tell you.

49:40.644 --> 49:41.728
What was it?

49:53.281 --> 49:54.533
What did you say?

49:55.325 --> 49:56.451
You heard me.

49:58.620 --> 50:01.832
No, I couldn't hear you. Tell me again.

50:04.084 --> 50:05.210
I love you.

50:09.756 --> 50:10.799
Do you…

50:14.052 --> 50:17.264
Do you even know
how long it took for you to say that?

50:18.932 --> 50:22.894
Why didn't you ever tell me this before?

50:24.563 --> 50:27.065
I love you, Yeon-su.

50:30.318 --> 50:32.654
You're such an idiot.

50:34.239 --> 50:37.409
You should say that face-to-face.
You're unbelievable.

50:38.160 --> 50:38.994
Fine.

50:39.619 --> 50:40.996
Then look behind you.

51:39.346 --> 51:40.514
You…

51:41.640 --> 51:42.557
Kook Yeon-su.

51:46.186 --> 51:47.395
I love you.

52:00.826 --> 52:02.285
What are you doing here?

52:02.911 --> 52:05.455
I missed you too much,
so I couldn't help it.

52:06.623 --> 52:08.375
But this is so sudden.

52:09.000 --> 52:11.253
I had to tell you this right now.

52:18.677 --> 52:22.472
Hey, long-distance relationships
are harder than I thought.

52:22.556 --> 52:24.975
That's why you should hurry and come back.

52:25.600 --> 52:27.435
Can you not skip a year?

52:28.019 --> 52:29.396
I don't know.

52:29.479 --> 52:33.400
You should study harder
and try to graduate early.

52:33.483 --> 52:35.360
You can't keep doing this.

52:35.443 --> 52:37.362
It'll take ages for you to graduate.

52:37.445 --> 52:40.198
Yeon-su, do you seriously
want to nag me right now?

52:40.282 --> 52:42.868
I'm only saying this for our sake.

52:57.173 --> 52:58.675
There were also times…

53:02.804 --> 53:07.017
that were
unbelievably phenomenal like this.

53:31.541 --> 53:35.128
That's why we could stay strong
during those years.

53:39.758 --> 53:42.218
And just like he promised,

53:42.302 --> 53:45.680
it didn't take him too long to come back.

53:52.896 --> 53:57.859
2 YEARS LATER

54:05.200 --> 54:06.242
Sol-i.

54:06.743 --> 54:07.661
Sol-i.

54:09.996 --> 54:11.873
- Hey, you.
- Look at you.

54:12.540 --> 54:16.002
- Where are your manners?
- We need to hurry. We're late.

54:16.086 --> 54:17.295
Did Ung's parents leave already?

54:17.379 --> 54:20.173
Yes, they left already. We need to hurry.

54:20.256 --> 54:21.341
Move aside.

54:25.845 --> 54:27.138
Have you been working out?

54:27.222 --> 54:30.684
What? That was nothing.
Wrap it up and come out.

54:30.767 --> 54:32.227
- I'll go start the car.
- Okay.

54:37.983 --> 54:40.694
That kid is really toying with me.

54:42.070 --> 54:43.905
He definitely has a crush on me,

54:43.989 --> 54:45.740
so why won't he make his move? Why?

54:45.824 --> 54:47.158
Come out already.

54:47.242 --> 54:48.201
Darn it.

54:48.994 --> 54:50.412
You're quite impudent.

54:51.413 --> 54:54.040
I didn't know
Mr. Choi's parents were this admirable.

54:54.124 --> 54:57.210
They must've spent a hefty sum
if they've been donating regularly.

54:57.877 --> 55:00.588
You're right.
I didn't know about this either,

55:00.672 --> 55:02.757
so I'm in awe.

55:04.259 --> 55:06.094
Will Ms. Kook be there too?

55:06.177 --> 55:07.637
She will.

55:08.388 --> 55:11.808
Will you be okay?
After all, she broke your heart.

55:13.810 --> 55:15.520
You never fail to remind me of that.

55:15.603 --> 55:18.106
Thank you. I'll never forget it.

55:20.025 --> 55:23.737
People say you're becoming more like me,
but you don't need to do this. Okay?

55:26.322 --> 55:27.407
Ji-ung.

55:27.490 --> 55:28.742
What is it this time?

55:29.325 --> 55:32.203
I'm only saying this
because you seem to be doing better now.

55:35.040 --> 55:36.207
I like you.

55:37.709 --> 55:40.712
I'm only saying this because people say
I'm becoming more like you.

55:42.088 --> 55:43.882
But you never told her how you feel.

55:45.633 --> 55:47.093
I don't want to be like that.

55:51.431 --> 55:53.516
I'm just saying.

56:08.740 --> 56:09.866
BOOK DONATION WITH UNG

56:10.617 --> 56:11.701
TWOO TWIT
THE RED DOG OF THE DARK

56:11.785 --> 56:14.871
WITH UNG

56:18.208 --> 56:20.126
Guys, it's ready.

56:23.588 --> 56:26.800
Sol-i, what are we having for dinner?

56:26.883 --> 56:28.218
Why all of a sudden?

56:28.301 --> 56:29.719
I'm asking you out on a date.

56:29.803 --> 56:31.763
BOOK DONATION WITH UNG

56:32.472 --> 56:33.473
I'm ready.

56:36.267 --> 56:37.977
So that's why he's been working out.

56:41.064 --> 56:43.483
Okay. It's nice to meet you.

56:43.566 --> 56:46.069
I'm a bit embarrassed.
This is nothing grand.

56:46.152 --> 56:49.948
As a member of society,

56:50.031 --> 56:52.992
I'm just doing what I should. Just a bit.

56:53.076 --> 56:54.828
Goodness, I'm embarrassed.

56:54.911 --> 56:57.205
Our son loved to read.

56:57.288 --> 56:59.624
As a boy, he'd always be reading.

56:59.707 --> 57:02.335
I think he takes after me.

57:03.002 --> 57:06.256
- I hope all kids can read as much as--
- Hey, Ung.

57:06.339 --> 57:07.465
Come on.

57:07.549 --> 57:10.051
You're late.
I told you to come early and help out.

57:10.135 --> 57:12.595
I've been here since this morning,
moving these books.

57:12.679 --> 57:13.930
- Really?
- Yes.

57:14.013 --> 57:17.684
We always need to do a retake
whenever Ung is here.

57:17.767 --> 57:19.769
Hey, did you stay up all night again?

57:19.853 --> 57:21.229
How long do you marinate pork?

57:21.312 --> 57:22.522
I don't know. Eight hours?

57:22.605 --> 57:24.941
I slept for ten hours.
That's longer than marinated pork.

57:25.024 --> 57:27.444
- What a good boy!
- Hello.

57:27.527 --> 57:28.736
- Hey, Yeon-su.
- Yeon-su.

57:28.820 --> 57:30.697
I told you not to come.

57:30.780 --> 57:32.407
You should rest on the weekend.

57:32.490 --> 57:34.826
I'm okay. I should help out.
Where do I put this?

57:34.909 --> 57:36.119
Upstairs.

57:36.202 --> 57:38.204
- Yeon-su, just make Ung carry that too.
- Go.

57:38.288 --> 57:39.330
Hurry.

57:41.958 --> 57:45.336
BOOK DONATION WITH UNG

57:56.222 --> 57:58.224
Don't you think you're sleeping
too much these days?

57:58.308 --> 58:01.060
Once the exhibition begins,
I won't be getting enough sleep.

58:01.144 --> 58:02.937
I should sleep while I can.

58:03.646 --> 58:05.940
Gosh, when will we put all these books in?

58:06.024 --> 58:09.402
Don't put them in wherever.
Arrange them in order.

58:09.486 --> 58:10.653
I'll be watching you.

58:25.251 --> 58:29.464
Doesn't this remind you of high school?

58:29.547 --> 58:31.841
Wasn't that so long ago?

58:32.842 --> 58:36.513
No. It still feels like yesterday to me.

58:38.181 --> 58:40.141
Frankly, I feel the same.

58:45.563 --> 58:46.731
Tell me the truth.

58:47.315 --> 58:48.191
About what?

58:48.775 --> 58:51.819
You had a crush on me
ever since we first met, right?

58:53.738 --> 58:56.199
There you go, manipulating
your memory again.

58:56.908 --> 58:58.117
What?

58:58.201 --> 59:00.912
No, I could see it in your eyes.

59:00.995 --> 59:03.540
Hey, don't make me laugh.

59:03.623 --> 59:06.376
Are you sure you didn't fall in love
with me at first sight?

59:06.459 --> 59:08.670
That's why you followed me around.

59:09.254 --> 59:11.297
When did I see you for the first time?

59:11.881 --> 59:13.216
Was it the first day of filming?

59:13.883 --> 59:15.635
- Hey.
- Or was it before that?

59:17.011 --> 59:19.973
I know you're pretending not to remember.

59:37.448 --> 59:40.952
Hey, why haven't you been putting
the books in?

59:41.035 --> 59:42.787
Why would you doodle on that?

59:42.870 --> 59:44.122
You're not a kid.

59:44.205 --> 59:45.540
I LOVE EARLY SUMMER
LEE NA-EUN

59:46.165 --> 59:47.625
What did you draw?

59:56.342 --> 59:57.677
Everyone has

59:58.678 --> 01:00:01.264
unforgettable memories
from a certain year of their life.

01:00:06.394 --> 01:00:09.022
They cherish those memories so much

01:00:09.772 --> 01:00:11.232
that it lasts a lifetime.

01:00:16.279 --> 01:00:17.280
Yeon-su.

01:00:20.408 --> 01:00:22.410
And our year…

01:00:38.301 --> 01:00:39.927
hasn't ended yet.

01:00:43.306 --> 01:00:45.391
Will you marry me?

01:00:47.352 --> 01:00:53.399
EPILOGUE

01:01:00.782 --> 01:01:01.991
Let's shoot a documentary.

01:01:04.535 --> 01:01:06.746
What? What did you just say?

01:01:07.246 --> 01:01:08.706
You have to.

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:10.500
Are you crazy? Why would we?

01:01:11.793 --> 01:01:14.253
Your last documentary is trending again.

01:01:14.337 --> 01:01:15.963
Why did you have to get married?

01:01:16.047 --> 01:01:17.924
People want to watch
your married life now.

01:01:18.007 --> 01:01:20.802
Are we not allowed to have any privacy?

01:01:20.885 --> 01:01:23.721
Hey, do you think
we're a pair of pushovers or something?

01:01:24.722 --> 01:01:25.890
- Hello.
- Hello.

01:01:25.973 --> 01:01:27.308
I'm Choi Ung.

01:01:28.476 --> 01:01:29.477
I'm Kook Yeon-su.

01:01:33.231 --> 01:01:34.399
One, two, three.

01:01:34.482 --> 01:01:36.234
- We're married.
- We're married.

01:01:41.906 --> 01:01:48.913
OUR BELOVED SUMMER

01:02:36.669 --> 01:02:41.674
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
